==============================================================================
A.  THE ASSUMED CHAIN   E_CRe/M_* = K_ep * eps_CR * E_SN / M_per_SN
==============================================================================

   A1  IMF factor, recomputed here from the IMF definitions
       (progenitor mass range 8-100 Msun, IMF integrated 0.1-100)
       IMF            Msun per CCSN    CCSN per 100 Msun
       Chabrier 2003  84.75            1.180
       Salpeter 1955  134.7            0.742
       -> the value 100 Msun/CCSN assumed in stage9_budget.py is the
          Chabrier result to 15%; Salpeter would give 135 Msun.

   A2  Chabrier 2003:
       E_SN/M_*  = 1.18e+49 erg/Msun
       E_CR/M_*  = 1.18e+48 erg/Msun   (eps_CR = 0.10)
       E_CRe/M_* = 1.18e+46 erg/Msun   (K_ep   = 0.01)

   A2  Salpeter 1955:
       E_SN/M_*  = 7.42e+48 erg/Msun
       E_CR/M_*  = 7.42e+47 erg/Msun   (eps_CR = 0.10)
       E_CRe/M_* = 7.42e+45 erg/Msun   (K_ep   = 0.01)

==============================================================================
B.  OBSERVATIONAL ANCHOR -- the Milky Way (measured, not assumed)
==============================================================================

   Strong et al. (2010) ApJL 722, L58, Table 2 -- INJECTED CR
   luminosity, 0.1-100 GeV, six propagation models [erg/s]:
     total CR      6.6e+40 - 8.05e+40   (headline value 7.9e40)
     protons       6.01e+40 - 7.37e+40
     primary e-    8.65e+38 - 1.34e+39

   => MEASURED injection-power ratio K_ep = L(prim e-)/L(p)
      = 0.0119 - 0.0212   (assumed in stage9_budget.py: 0.01)

   Licquia & Newman (2015) ApJ 806, 96:  SFR(MW) = 1.65 +/- 0.19 Msun/yr

   => ENERGY INJECTED PER SOLAR MASS OF STAR FORMATION [erg/Msun]
      all cosmic rays      1.26e+48 - 1.54e+48  (+/- 12% from SFR)
      cosmic-ray ELECTRONS 1.65e+46 - 2.56e+46  (+/- 12% from SFR)
      -> full range including the SFR error: 1.5e+46 - 2.9e+46 erg/Msun
      -> best single value: 2.1e+46 erg/Msun

==============================================================================
C.  COMPARISON AND VERDICT
==============================================================================

   quantity [erg/Msun]                assumed          measured (MW)    ratio
   all cosmic rays                    1e+48            1.44e+48         1.44
   cosmic-ray electrons               1e+46            2.07e+46         2.07

   The assumed value is LOW by a factor 2.1, i.e. conservative
   in the direction that matters (it understates the CR electron
   contribution).  Redoing the stage9 comparison with the measured
   value:
t(z=10.0) = 471.4 Myr    t(z=5.5) = 1038.5 Myr    Delta t = 567.0 Myr
F_KN:  b=1e-04->9.994e-01   b=1e-01->6.345e-01   b=1e+00->1.473e-01   b=1e+02->3.045e-04
Tablas colisionales listas (n=2..10, 700 nodos).
Raices de Planck:  x_max=8.1723   x_min=0.2278
     CR electrons / UV, assumed  = 6.50e-05
     CR electrons / UV, measured = 1.34e-04  (range 9.5e-05 - 1.9e-04)
   The conclusion is unchanged: cosmic-ray electrons deliver ~1e-4
   of the ionizations that escaping stellar UV does.

   CAVEAT, flagged: the Milky Way anchor is a present-day,
   high-metallicity, strongly magnetised disc.  At z ~ 10 the SN
   energy per Msun is plausibly HIGHER (top-heavy IMF, more massive
   progenitors) and the CR escape fraction into the IGM larger
   (Leite et al. 2017 MNRAS 469, 416).  Both push the same way and
   neither is a factor 1e4.  A factor 10 enhancement would still
   leave CR electrons at ~1e-3 of the UV ionizations.
